WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.720
Please welcome the one and only,

2
00:00:01.720 --> 00:00:04.128
the funny, the brilliant Craig Robinson.

3
00:00:04.128 --> 00:00:07.128
(audience cheering)

4
00:00:09.452 --> 00:00:10.285
Hi!

5
00:00:12.729 --> 00:00:14.606
Hello, how are you?

6
00:00:14.606 --> 00:00:16.941
I'm so happy that you're here.

7
00:00:16.941 --> 00:00:18.848
And I'm so glad to be here, thank you for having me.

8
00:00:18.848 --> 00:00:21.379
Please have a sit.

9
00:00:21.379 --> 00:00:22.810
Hey, hey, hey!

10
00:00:22.810 --> 00:00:23.977
Hey, hey, hey!

11
00:00:25.286 --> 00:00:26.119
Hello!

12
00:00:27.232 --> 00:00:30.730
Craig, when did you burst onto the scene?

13
00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:34.500
Because I could swear it was easily 40 something years ago.

14
00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:37.750
Like I don't remember life without you.

15
00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:39.807
But sometimes when I look at your resume and I'm like,

16
00:00:39.807 --> 00:00:44.150
"Oh," like you didn't start 40 something years ago.

17
00:00:44.150 --> 00:00:48.900
I got to Hollywood in 1999.

18
00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:52.640 line:15%
And then, I think "The Office" was about 2004.

19
00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:55.540 line:15%
Well, that is a long time ago now if you think about it.

20
00:00:57.020 --> 00:00:59.481
But you did stand-up.

21
00:00:59.481 --> 00:01:00.710
I do stand-up still.

22
00:01:00.710 --> 00:01:01.758
I mean, yeah exactly.

23
00:01:01.758 --> 00:01:02.591
Yeah, yeah.

24
00:01:02.591 --> 00:01:05.591
(audience clapping)

25
00:01:06.603 --> 00:01:09.900
And is it true that there's something

26
00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:14.206
like of a story of stand-up X a rubber chicken?

27
00:01:14.206 --> 00:01:15.039
Oh yeah.

28
00:01:15.039 --> 00:01:18.070
Oh, when I was getting started,

29
00:01:18.070 --> 00:01:20.310
there was this place in Chicago

30
00:01:21.230 --> 00:01:23.350
they had a night called Heckler's Heaven.

31
00:01:23.350 --> 00:01:28.080
And you got three minutes, okay, of nobody bothering you.

32
00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:31.500
And then, you had eight minutes total

33
00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:32.900
if you didn't get a rubber chicken.

34
00:01:32.900 --> 00:01:35.270
Three people in the audience had a rubber chicken.

35
00:01:35.270 --> 00:01:38.120
So once that three-minute bell hit,

36
00:01:38.120 --> 00:01:40.540
if somebody wants to throw the rubber chicken at you,

37
00:01:40.540 --> 00:01:42.020
you had to get off stage.

38
00:01:42.020 --> 00:01:44.990
And I got two rubber chickens,

39
00:01:44.990 --> 00:01:47.820
I said, "I'm not getting a third," so I got off.

40
00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:50.470
And then, the next week I came back with my keyboard

41
00:01:50.470 --> 00:01:51.800
and that's all she wrote,

42
00:01:51.800 --> 00:01:53.685
and now do stand-up with the keyboard.

43
00:01:53.685 --> 00:01:57.327
(audience clapping)

44
00:01:57.327 --> 00:01:59.990
I guess it like sharpens your skills.

45
00:01:59.990 --> 00:02:01.950
Well, it certainly keeps you on your toes,

46
00:02:01.950 --> 00:02:04.290
yeah, to get to the jokes.

47
00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:07.650
Is it true that you have written yourself notes

48
00:02:08.970 --> 00:02:12.240
about kind of where you wanna go in life,

49
00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:14.390
and if so, why do you do that?

50
00:02:14.390 --> 00:02:16.013
I love this.

51
00:02:18.616 --> 00:02:19.530
When I was in college

52
00:02:19.530 --> 00:02:23.280
that's when I felt like comedy chose me.

53
00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:26.140
And I wrote a note to myself 'cause I knew

54
00:02:26.140 --> 00:02:27.400
I was getting into comedy.

55
00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:29.660
And I said, "You are going to be a great comedian,"

56
00:02:29.660 --> 00:02:31.747
and I crossed out, "going to be."

57
00:02:32.620 --> 00:02:34.700
I said, "You are a great comedian."

58
00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:38.103
I really think that words matter.

59
00:02:39.740 --> 00:02:40.664
Absolutely.

60
00:02:40.664 --> 00:02:43.400
And a turn of phrase, a choice of words,

61
00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:47.290
pulling out going to be rather than I am.

62
00:02:47.290 --> 00:02:52.290
Those things I think are like inextricably linked

63
00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:54.082
with belief.
Yeah, in sinks in for sure.

64
00:02:54.082 --> 00:02:56.665 line:15%
(upbeat music)

